3.1.2.2 Elemental Survey:
The different elements present in the CuFeBTC/S-GNS nanocomposite were identified by employing EDS technique. The EDS sum spectrum comprising all the elements of hybrid nanocomposite with their corresponding element maps have been recorded from this study and are shown in Fig. 2(A-F). Fig. 2(A) depicts the focused SEM region of the CuFeBTC/S-GNS composite which looks tinged specifying the presence of all the elements. The elemental mapping images of the respective elements viz. C (red), O (yellow), S (green), Cu (purple) and Fe (blue) in the CuFeBTC/S-GNS composite are represented in Fig. 2(B-F). Also, it is significant from the sum spectrum that each of the aforementioned elements exhibit distinguished elemental peaks during EDS analysis (Fig. 2(G)). The atomic weight percentage obtained for each element in the CuFeBTC/S-GNS nanocomposite is listed in the table given inset of the EDS spectrum. Thus, the elemental mapping and EDS spectrum depicts the presence of all the elements in the CuFeBTC/S-GNS nanocomposite and ensures the successful doping of sulphur heteroatom on the exfoliated graphene layers.
